<title>DENMARK: Danish crown to fall slightly but remain stable - survey.</title>
<headline>Danish crown to fall slightly but remain stable - survey.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Danish crown will fall slightly but remain basically stable between 3.8097-3.8247 on average per mark in the next 12 months, according to a Reuter survey issued on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sixteen Danish and foreign banks and brokerage firms were asked in recent days to predict where exchange rates would be three, six and 12 months from now. They came up with the following average forecasts.</p>
<p>			    3-ths     6-mths   12-mths</p>
<p>Crowns per mark	 3.8097    3.8159   3.8247</p>
<p>The Danish crown traded at 3.8081 per mark at 1330 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Crowns per mark:</p>
<p>					  3-mths   6-mths   12-mths</p>
